            <ArticleTitle>Highly Enantioselective Synthesis of Chiral Cyclopropyl Nucleosides via Catalytic Asymmetric Intermolecular Cyclopropanation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6494-6497</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03110</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An efficient route to construct chiral cyclopropyl purine nucleoside analogues has been established via the catalytic asymmetric Michael-initiated ring-closure reactions of α-purine acrylates with α-bromo-carboxylic esters. Using (DHQD)2AQN as the catalyst, various chiral cyclopropyl purine nucleoside analogues with a chiral quaternary stereocenter were obtained in 72-98% yields, excellent diastereoselectivities, and 93-97% ee. Through simple functional group transformations, diverse chiral cyclopropyl purine nucleosides with hydroxymethyl group or carboxyl group were obtained.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
